# Line-ending policy.
#
# Every file committed to this repository uses LF — HEAD is LF end to end.
# Windows editors had been rewriting working-tree files to CRLF, which buried
# real changes under thousands of line-ending-only diff lines.
#
#   text=auto  git detects text vs binary and stores text with LF in the repo
#   eol=lf     text files are checked out with LF regardless of core.autocrlf
#
# This keeps diffs honest without forcing anyone to reconfigure their editor:
# a working-tree file saved as CRLF no longer registers as a change.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never transform these.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
